1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
 There's one habit silently destroying your workouts,

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,840
 and it has nothing to do with how hard you train.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,800
 I've seen it over and over again in the gym.

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:10,580
 Someone walks in, full of energy, ready to crush their workout session.

5
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:13,460
 And then, a text, a quick scroll through Instagram, a juicy DM,

6
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,600
 and suddenly, half their focus is gone.

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,720
 I've been there too, thinking, eh, one quick check won't hurt.

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,760
 Here's the science behind what's actually happening.

9
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,320
 Studies show that even shortfall interruptions trigger what's called a cognitive switch.

10
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,300
 It not only spikes your cortisol, but also disrupts the precious mind-muscle connection.

11
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,100
 And here's the kicker.

12
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:30,940
 Scrolling primes your brain for dopamine.

13
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:34,660
 You go from effortless dopamine hits to suddenly demanding full focus

14
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,920
 on something that's actually really hard, like lifting weights.

15
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:39,040
 No wonder your workouts feel draining.

16
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:40,520
 So use this knowledge to your advantage.

17
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:44,940
 If you're mentally exhausted, recognize that your phone may be the source of dopamine depletion

18
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:45,800
 and cognitive switch.

19
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:49,640
 Use the workout time to dial in, digital detox, and go ham.

20
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,680
 You've done harder things in life than putting away your phone.

21
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:52,960
 You got this.

